Header: the 2025 logo, and a menu that stays on the bar at every width

The hamburger and its drawer are gone, and so is `nav.js`. Every menu link is on the bar at every width,
one tap from any page. As the bar narrows, things give up their room in this order:

1. What's on Channel 97 goes first, at 60rem (unchanged).
2. Join and Submit (`menu_folds` in `_config.yml`) keep only their icons, at 52rem.
3. Every item but the page you are on keeps only its icon, at 36rem. The four main words last to about
   600px, which the measurements bear out: the name and the menu with its words need 566px.
4. On a phone (30rem) the menu takes its own row under the name. The header is 103px tall there, and
   `--head-h` follows so the hero still fills the rest.

The page you are on always keeps its icon, its word (in the menu's sans, not the masthead's serif)
and its yellow underline. That replaces `.site-head-here`, the serif page name the drawer used to leave
behind. A word that is hidden is still the link's accessible name. Icon-only links get a little more
icon and padding, as a thumb's target.

Merge qualifications:
- [x] The logo at 1280, 600 and 390: no overflow; the tabs stop at the masthead's bottom edge (68/69px, and
      102/103px on a phone)
- [x] `jekyll build` clean; tokens, secrets, internal-publish and no-code guards pass
- [x] Measured in headless Firefox at 1280, 1000, 900, 840, 760, 700, 672, 600, 520, 480, 430, 390 and
      360: nothing overflows the bar or the page at any of them
- [x] A folded item keeps its word when it is the page (/submit/ at 760, /join/ at 600). The home page on
      a phone is icons only, and every link keeps its name.
- [ ] Playwright: the drawer tests are rewritten. `smoke.spec.js` checks every link is on screen at 1280,
      820, 600 and 390, with the current page's word visible and no sideways scroll. `onair.spec.js`
      checks the current page's word instead of the drawer button. They first run in CI.

**The mark:** the 2025 logo (`brand/2025.png`) stands in for the yellow square until the board picks the
new one. `site/assets/img/logo-2025.png` is the same art trimmed to its pixels (192×192 to 168×103), so it
sits as a landscape, 2.35rem tall (61×38 on screen) and as tall as the name's two lines. The name moves
right to make room. The main words still last to 600px with it. On the dark band the logo's black
outlines and the camera's handle mostly disappear; the coloured body and its lettering carry it.

**/reserve/'s tabs on a phone** stick under the masthead (`top: var(--head-h)`) instead of sliding behind
it.

